{"duration_api_ms":815515,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b3582635-083d-4d21-a877-4ec6aedfc636","total_cost_usd":26.639940999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":312106,"cache_read_input_tokens":41463994,"output_tokens":75987,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22592},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":312106,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4209,"cache_read_input_tokens":403315,"cache_creation_input_tokens":324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":324},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":290,"outputTokens":76772,"thinkingTokens":22763,"cacheReadInputTokens":41490602,"cacheCreationInputTokens":397389,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":26.639940999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":205,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All 21 findings are handled: 20 with code changes and Finding 19 with no change, because a probe showed the failure can't happen. `dart analyze lib test` reports 0 errors and 0 warnings; the 36 info-level lints are all in files I didn't touch. `flutter test` passes 62/62. No git mutations. I deleted my probe and scratch files, and left the files that were already in the scratchpad alone.\n\n## 1. What changed, per finding\n\n- **F1 (settings import/reset flips login mode):** Importing settings (`storage.dart`) and \"重置可导出的设置\" (`about/view.dart`) now keep this device's current `loginMode`. A backup therefore can't switch it on or off. `MineController._onLogoutMain` no longer deletes the account unless login mode is on and `Accounts.main` is a `LoginAccount`. An anonymized request that answers \"账号未登录\" can't delete stored credentials any more.\n- **F2 (missing account-only endpoints):** Added to `_accountApis`:\n  - `Api.favResourceList` and `Api.mediaList`\n  - `Api.setLiveFavTag`\n  - `${appBaseUrl}/x/v2/account/myinfo`\n  - `/x/member/app/{uname,sign,sex,birthday}/update`\n\n  Each one has a test in `login_policy_test.dart`. I used no generic access_key rule, and `feedDislike` is untouched.\n- **F3 (incognito badge follows the heartbeat role):** `anonymity` now comes only from `!loginMode`. I removed the three places that reset it from `heartbeat.isLogin`: `accounts.dart`, which also loses the now-unused `MineController` import, plus `login/controller.dart` and `about/view.dart`.\n- **F4 (UP space always shows \"not followed\"):** In login mode, the space page now fetches `UserHttp.userRelation(mid)` (on the allowlist) when the space isn't your own. The relation shows `-10` for special follows, and blacklist status comes through the attribute.\n- **F5 (live danmaku socket sends your uid):** The socket now always sends `uid: 0`, because its token is fetched anonymously.\n- **F6 (WebView gets the full login cookies):**\n  - New `LoginUtils.setAnonymousWebCookie()`. It deletes every stored account's cookies from the WebView and installs the anonymous jar. Startup (`init.dart`) and `onLoginMain` use it.\n  - The \"重置cookie\" menu still installs the account's cookies, because it's an explicit user action.\n  - Taking notes is treated as an account flow:\n    - Non-Linux: the account's cookies go in before the page loads (the body waits for them) and are removed again when the page closes.\n    - Linux: `openLinux` injects the account's cookies only for the note-app URL, and the anonymous jar everywhere else.\n- **F7 (extras request bursts and the deletion race):**\n  - Extras exports now run one at a time from a queue in `DownloadService`.\n  - `DownloadExtras.export` takes a `cancelled` check, polled between steps, comment pages, reply pages and subtitles.\n  - `deleteDownload` and `deletePage` cancel the export and wait for it if it's already running.\n  - `CommentImages` creates its folder non-recursively, so it can't recreate a deleted video folder.\n  - An export folder holding only `.part` files (left behind if the app was killed mid-merge) is reused instead of creating \"name (2)\". Folders a merge is writing into right now are excluded.\n  - Self-test waits for the extras (5-minute cap) before it reports `folderFiles`.\n  - The 200/10 comment defaults are unchanged.\n- **F8 (416 truncation, retry budget):**\n  - A 416 with no usable `Content-Range` now asks for the size with a 1-byte range request.\n  - If the size still can't be found, the attempt fails without truncating the file.\n  - Only consecutive attempts that save nothing count toward the 6-attempt budget, and the backoff follows that count.\n- **F9 (merge guard shared across merges):** `_mergingCid` / `_mergeDeleted` became per-entry sets: `_mergingCids` and `_mergeDeletedCids`.\n- **F10 (old-format merge picks segments from disk):** The segment count now comes from `index.json`'s `segment_list`. Higher-numbered leftover segments are deleted. If `index.json` can't be read, the old probing is the fallback.\n- **F11 (multi-segment fallback):**\n  - Any remux/join error, not only `UnsupportedError`, now falls back to keeping the segments.\n  - Each part's extension comes from its content (flv, mp4, ts, else `.bin`), including the single-file case.\n  - Android media-scans every part, not just the first.\n  - A toast says when segments are saved separately.\n  - Merge failure sets `DownloadStatus.failMerge`.\n  - In-app playback of the separate parts is untouched (deferred).\n- **F12 (live room, logged out):** The input bar now shows when you're logged out. It keeps the danmaku toggle and hides like and send.\n- **F13 (file paths as launch arguments):** The link stream now opens existing local paths and `file:` URIs as files instead of routing them. It skips the file `main()` already opened (`PiliScheme.launchFile`) and the app's own executable path.\n- **F14 (XML danmaku from other tools):**\n  - `<base>.xml` is used when `<base>.danmaku.xml` doesn't exist.\n  - The parser accepts other attributes, `p=` anywhere in the tag, and single quotes.\n  - Numeric entities are decoded in a single pass.\n  - Test added.\n- **F15 (local feed refetches everyone):** Uploads are cached per UP for the session (30 minutes). Opening the tab or following/unfollowing someone fetches only uncached or stale UPs. Pull-to-refresh still fetches everyone.\n- **F16 (self-test isolation):** The self-test uses its own temp subfolder on every platform. On Linux, `--selftest` sets `G_APPLICATION_NON_UNIQUE`, so it runs as its own instance instead of being forwarded.\n- **F17 (heartbeats for local playback):** `makeHeartBeat` returns early for any file source, which covers offline downloads and plain local files.\n- **F18 (favourites panel):** If the account folders fail to load, the local folders still show above the error. \"完成\" then saves only the local choice and closes.\n- **F19 (Windows long paths):** No change. A real Dart probe wrote, renamed and listed a 309-character path successfully, then cleaned up. `dart.exe` has no `longPathAware` manifest, so the machine's `LongPathsEnabled=1` setting didn't apply to the probe. dart:io adds the `\\\\?\\` prefix itself, so the failure can't happen there.\n- **F20 (library import clears before checking):** New `LocalLibrary.checkImport`. It parses every entry with the same parsers the app uses, and throws before anything is cleared. It runs both inside `importAll` and before settings import touches any box.\n- **F21 (update dialog):** Removed the Windows \"exe\" button; only \"zip\" remains.\n\n## 2. `git diff`\n\nThe full diff is 1,567 lines, too long to paste here. It's saved at `C:\\Users\\Z14\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-Z14-Documents-Coding-Piliplus\\b3582635-083d-4d21-a877-4ec6aedfc636\\tool-results\\bw7pyal6w.txt`. It's identical to `git diff -- lib linux test` on the working tree now; please give that exact output to the re-review.\n\nFiles touched:\n- `lib/http/init.dart`\n- `lib/main.dart`\n- `lib/pages/{about/view, danmaku/controller, fav_panel/view, live_room/controller, live_room/view, local/feed, login/controller, member/controller, mine/controller, webview/view}.dart`\n- `lib/plugin/pl_player/controller.dart`\n- `lib/services/download/{download_extras, download_manager, download_service}.dart`\n- `lib/services/local_library.dart`\n- `lib/utils/{accounts, accounts/login_policy, app_scheme, login_utils, path_utils, self_test, storage, update}.dart`\n- `linux/runner/my_application.cc`\n- `test/utils/{download_extras_test, login_policy_test}.dart`\n\n`audit-logs/route-pending.md` shows as modified, but that edit isn't mine.\n\n## 3. Uncertainties\n\n- **F1:**\n  - I chose to keep the current login mode rather than re-apply accounts after import. As a result, a backup's `loginMode` is never restored.\n  - `hideInteraction` from an import only takes effect on screens built afterwards.\n- **F2:**\n  - `favResourceList` and `mediaList` now carry the account in login mode for every folder, including other users' public folders. The alternative in the finding was matching your own folder ids.\n  - The server error codes are unverified; nothing was sent to the network.\n- **F4:** \"被关注\" (`isFollowed`) still comes from the anonymous space data.\n- **F6:**\n  - The note flow is my reading of \"explicit account flow\". If the note page is closed abnormally, its cookies stay until the next start or login.\n  - After \"重置cookie\", the account's cookies remain in the WebView until the next start or login.\n  - Linux has no step to delete old cookies, because `setAnonymousWebCookie` returns early on Linux.\n- **F7:** A cancelled export can still finish the one request or image download it's in the middle of before it stops.\n- **F8:** On a CDN that answers the 1-byte probe without a size, a finished segment now fails after 6 attempts with its bytes kept, where before it was truncated and downloaded again.\n- **F11:**\n  - Content that's neither flv, mp4 nor ts is now saved as `.bin`, which galleries won't play.\n  - `failMerge` is set only in memory; entry status isn't saved to disk.\n- **F13:**\n  - What package:gtk actually delivers is unverified. I can't run Linux here.\n  - The `.desktop` file (`%u`, no video MIME types) is unchanged.\n- **F14:** A `data-p=` attribute would also match, which is harmless.\n- **F16:** `my_application.cc` is not compiled or tested here (no Linux toolchain).\n- **F17:** I turned off heartbeats for all offline playback, not just `cid == 0`. Watching downloads in login mode no longer syncs history.\n- **F18:** I also changed \"完成\" to skip the account request when the account folders failed to load. The finding didn't explicitly ask for that.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (+ dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source \".../scratchpad/tools/local_env.sh\" && cd \"$REPO\" && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 62\n  passed: 62\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~22000 (flutter test; dart analyze ~250000)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\nOne analyze run caught a compile error in my own code: collection-if isn't allowed in `path.join` arguments in `path_utils.dart`. I fixed it with `path.joinAll`, and the run above is clean.\n\nThe claude.ai Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors still need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and the `agentbridge` MCP server failed to connect. None of them were needed here.","ttft_ms":3471,"type":"result","duration_ms":1597847,"uuid":"65995eeb-3243-4046-b2b6-1477aaf57f9e","ttft_stream_ms":3183,"time_to_request_ms":557,"first_content_frame_ms":3183,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
